## webview Optional Extras Module (feature-gated)
##
## Part of the Alya Language package ecosystem (https://github.com/alya-lang).
## Demonstrates feature-gated API slices: this module is only compiled when
## the `extras` feature is active (see `[features]` in `alya.toml`). Gate
## imports and items with `@cfg(feature = "...")` and keep a
## `@cfg(not(feature = "..."))` fallback stub in `src/lib.alya` so callers
## get a clear descriptive error instead of an undefined reference.

## Returns an enthusiastic greeting for the specified recipient.
##
## Only available when the `extras` feature is active (default-on). Without
## it, the fallback stub in `src/lib.alya` throws a descriptive error.
##
## ### Parameters
## - `name`: The recipient name string. Defaults to `"World"`.
##
## ### Returns
## The greeting string `"Howdy, {name}!"`.
##
## ### Examples
## ```alya
## let msg = extra_greeting("Alya") # "Howdy, Alya!"
## ```
@cfg(feature = "extras")
pub function extra_greeting(name = "World") -> string
    return "Howdy, {name}!"
end
